{"absent":["Numeric bit positions and mask values for page flags, change masks and table markers.","Locking, ordering and translation flush rules around concurrent table walks and updates.","Layouts for processor descriptors, memory descriptors and page descriptors.","Cache mode encoding and its mapping to protection values.","Full inverted frame number rules beyond directional stepping.","Behavior and failure handling of accounting hooks.","Five level enablement detection and level folding mechanics.","Processor feature detection implementation and shadow stack exception behavior."],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_young","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_dirty.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_dirty.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_young.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_young.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_young","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_write","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_write.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_write.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_write.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_write.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_huge","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_global","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_exec","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_special"],"text":"The interface provides read-only predicates over page table entry values that report hardware dirtiness, accessed youth, logical writability, large page presence, global visibility, executability and special handling. Parallel forms cover small pages and larger intermediate levels, each examining a supplied entry value and leaving table memory unchanged."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_trans_huge","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_trans_huge","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::has_transparent_hugepage.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::has_transparent_hugepage.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_special","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_special","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_uffd","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_uffd","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_soft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_soft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_soft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_protnone","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_protnone","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_accessible.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_accessible.alt_2"],"text":"Further predicates detect transparent huge page mappings, probe processor support for large pages, test special markers, user fault related state, software held dirtiness and protection none state, and judge accessibility with attention to pending invalidation work. These support reclamation, migration and fault handling policy."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_set_flags","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_clear_flags","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_clear_flags","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkclean","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkold","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkexec","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkyoung","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkwrite_novma","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkhuge","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkglobal","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_clrglobal","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkspecial","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkold","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkclean","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkyoung","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkwrite_novma","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkspecial","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkold","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkclean","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkyoung","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkspecial"],"text":"Basic constructors produce adjusted entry values that set or clear age, cleanliness, executability, global visibility, special handling and large page shape. They operate on values held by the caller and create new values for later installation, without themselves updating table memory."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkwrite","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkwrite","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkwrite","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkwrite_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkwrite_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mksaveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mksaveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mksaveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_clear_saveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_clear_saveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_clear_saveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::mksaveddirty_shift","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::clear_saveddirty_shift","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkuffd","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_clear_uffd","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkuffd","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_clear_uffd","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mksoft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mksoft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mksoft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_clear_soft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_clear_soft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_clear_soft_dirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkinvalid"],"text":"Write lifecycle constructors move entries among writable, shadow stack writable, protected, trapped, software dirty and invalid forms. Removal of writability relocates prior hardware dirtiness into software held storage, while installation of writability restores it, keeping protected entries distinct from shadow stack encodings."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgprot_noncached","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgprot_modify.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgprot_modify.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::p4d_pgprot","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::p4d_pfn","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgd_pfn","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_page","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::p4d_page","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgd_page","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_same","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_advance_pfn.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_advance_pfn.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pages_to_mb","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::PFN_PTE_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_pfn.alt_1"],"text":"Protection replacement merges an old entry with a new protection value while keeping hardware managed status from the old value and taking remaining protection from the new value, with guard handling for protection none transitions. Companion helpers force uncached type on capable processors, translate between frame numbers and page descriptors at each level, test entry equality, step a leaf entry across frames with awareness of inverted encoding, and scale page counts to megabytes."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgd_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::p4d_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_pte_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_pmd_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_pud_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_set_pte","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_set_pmd","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_set_pud","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::native_local_ptep_get_and_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::native_local_pmdp_get_and_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::native_local_pudp_get_and_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_ptep_get_and_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_get_and_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_get_and_clear_full","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_set_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_try_set.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_try_set.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::set_pmd_at","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::set_pud_at"],"text":"Table management primitives clear slots at each level, store fresh values through single volatile updates, and take a current value while clearing its slot. Checked installs perform accounting ahead of the store, full teardown uses a lightweight local take, and conditional install succeeds only when the slot still holds an empty value."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_shstk","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_write","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_write.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_write.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_write.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_write.alt_2"],"text":"Shadow stack status applies only when the related processor feature is active. Small pages use dirty without writable for this purpose, while larger levels additionally require the large page indication. Logical writability tests for small and mid levels accept shadow stack entries as writable despite a clear writable indication, while the largest intermediate test in this set looks only at the writable indication itself."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::mksaveddirty_shift","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::clear_saveddirty_shift","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mksaveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_clear_saveddirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkdirty"],"text":"Write removal shifts any hardware dirty indication into a software held position so the resulting read only value cannot be mistaken for a shadow stack value. Dirty marking asserts both hardware and software indications before the same shift, and write installation shifts the software held indication back. Protection replacement applies the forward or reverse shift based on prior writability."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgprot_modify.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgprot_modify.alt_2"],"text":"Protection replacement keeps a fixed subset of hardware managed bits from the prior value and accepts all other protection bits from the incoming value. Leaf and large page forms each use their own preservation and address masks during guard handling, so frame identity and status survive the change."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_accessible.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_accessible.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_protnone","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_protnone","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_bad","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_bad","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::p4d_bad","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgd_bad","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgd_present"],"text":"Accessibility holds for present entries and for protection none entries while invalidation work remains pending. Protection none means the corresponding marker is present without the present marker. Malformed table checks disregard benign user and accessed markers and may disregard the no-execute marker under isolation builds, while top level presence and validity reduce to constant outcomes when five level paging is inactive."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::arch_end_context_switch","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::arch_flush_lazy_mmu_mode","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::debug_checkwx_user.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::debug_checkwx_user.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptdump_check_wx","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::flush_tlb_fix_spurious_fault"],"text":"Context switch completion and lazy mode flushing are empty operations in this configuration. User write execute verification either delegates to a walk helper or does nothing according to build choice, and the top level check alias plus spurious fault handling follow the same delegate or empty pattern."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::PFN_PTE_SHIFT","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::KERNEL_PGD_BOUNDARY","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::KERNEL_PGD_PTRS","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PTE_SAME","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PTEP_SET_ACCESS_FLAGS","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PTEP_TEST_AND_CLEAR_YOUNG","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PTEP_CLEAR_YOUNG_FLUSH","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PTEP_GET_AND_CLEAR","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PTEP_GET_AND_CLEAR_FULL","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PTEP_SET_WRPROTECT","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::__HAVE_ARCH_PMDP_SET_ACCESS_FLAGS","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_leaf.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_leaf.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_pfn.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkwrite","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkwrite","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgprot_modify.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable-invert.h::_ASM_PGTABLE_INVERT_H","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::_ASM_X86_PGTABLE_H","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_try_set.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::has_transparent_hugepage.alt_1"],"text":"The leaf frame shift matches the architectural page shift, and kernel half geometry derives from the top level index of the direct map base. The routed set announces architecture ownership of entry comparison, access flag handling, youth testing and clearing with flush, and take while clearing, together with leaf and frame number override markers and header guards."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_same","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::p4d_pfn","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pgd_pfn","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_advance_pfn.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_advance_pfn.alt_2","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_ptep_get_and_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_try_set.alt_1"],"text":"Entries wrap a single scalar that fully determines identity, so equality reduces to scalar comparison. Frame numbers emerge from masking address portions and shifting by the page shift with level specific masks, and stepping moves the scalar by a count scaled with the leaf shift, subtracting for inverted encodings and adding otherwise."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkold","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkyoung","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkclean","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkold","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkyoung","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkclean","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkold","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkyoung","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkclean","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkdirty","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_mkwrite"],"text":"Age and dirtiness move through paired transitions where old clears accessed and young asserts it, clean clears hardware and software dirtiness and dirty asserts both subject to relocation, and protection changes route through relocation or restoration. Trapped state layers protection removal above a marker, while software dirtiness toggles independently."},{"kind":"entry_point","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::set_pmd_at","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::set_pud_at","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_get_and_clear","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_get_and_clear_full","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_set_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_try_set.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::arch_end_context_switch","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::arch_flush_lazy_mmu_mode"],"text":"Memory management entry points comprise checked installs at intermediate levels, accounted takes, fast takes for full teardown, conditional empty slot installs, and in place protection. Context completion and lazy flush hooks remain available as stable call sites even while empty."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pte_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pmd_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::pud_modify","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_set_wrprotect","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable.h::ptep_try_set.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/pgtable_64.h::native_ptep_get_and_clear"],"text":"Clearing writability without care can create the shadow stack pattern when hardware dirtiness is already asserted, and hardware may assert dirtiness concurrently with software protection work. The affected paths therefore relocate dirtiness and use atomic compare exchange loops for in